=== CONTROLS ===
C1a Jaccard sees both prefix pairs at >= 0.50                   : False   <-- FIRES, and correctly: 0.44 on the second pair
C1b containment sees both prefix pairs at 1.00                  : True
C2 real pairing beats random re-pairing by more than 2x         : True (0.327 vs 0.024)
C3 every exact match is a heading the standing shape dictates   : True

The metric lesson, which the control produced rather than the analysis:
a SYMMETRIC similarity reports a subsumption as a partial match, so it is the
wrong instrument for a prefix relation. Containment is the right one and it
returns 1.00 on both pairs. Jaccard is kept beside it because it is the honest
answer to 'how similar are these two headings' and containment is the honest
answer to 'did one file's framing arrive inside the other's'.

RESULT: identity finds 2 matches and all are dictated; overlap finds
7 pairs at or above 0.50 including the two prefix relations, against a
null of 0.024. The shared premise set fixes a measurable amount of the
shape, and the number to quote is the overlap rather than an identity count.
